# Bricks Design System — color bible (non-negotiable)

Companion to `bricks-ds-all-tokens` (radius, spacing, type, text styles — same law).

**Source of truth (v1.2.0):** `design-system/tokens/`  
**Archive:** `design-system/archives/bricks_design_system_tokens_v1_2_0.zip`  
**CSS bridge (consumers only):** `design-system/tokens.css` (`--ds-*` vars)

These tokens are the bible. **Never ever** introduce, invent, approximate, or hardcode any UI color outside this set — not in CSS, React, Figma canvas/`figma-cli`, mocks, or one-off “just for this screen” fills.

## Allowed colors only

Primitives live in `design-system/tokens/color_primitives.Value.tokens.json` (families: `purple`, `warm_neutral`, `grey_neutral`, `pink`, `blue`, `yellow`, `green`, `red`, `pistachio_sand`, `lavender_mist`, `soft_butter`).

Semantic/alias tokens live in `design-system/tokens/color_tokens.Value.tokens.json` — prefer these for UI roles when they exist.

In code/CSS: use existing `--ds-*` variables from `tokens.css` only.  
In Figma: bind to **Bricks Design System** library variables only (no new local variables).

## Hard bans

- **No new hex/rgb/hsl** — if it isn’t in the v1.2.0 token files, it does not ship.
- **No “close enough”** palette picks, gradients made from off-token stops, or opacity hacks meant to fake a missing color (opacity on a DS color is fine when the base token is DS).
- **No creating** new color variables, new text styles, or text-style variables to work around gaps.
- If nothing in the bible fits → **stop and ask**. Do not extend the DS unless the user explicitly requests a token update.

## Before painting anything

1. Look up the token in `design-system/tokens/` (or `--ds-*` in `tokens.css`).
2. Use / bind that token.
3. Never invent an ID, name, or hex from memory.
